  "final_message": "I have launched the test suite to verify the baseline build and tests, and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for the test suite to finish execution.\nWaiting for the architecture check to complete.\nI cannot drop `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly:\n- **External Consumers**: While `channel` is not read elsewhere inside `orders-service`, the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event is published to the `orders.placed` topic and consumed by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Dropping this field is a breaking change for downstream consumers.\n- **Model Requirement**: As long as [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) requires `channel`, the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) models must retain it so [`orderPlaced()`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) can populate the event.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\nTo retire the field according to architecture rules:\n1. Announce deprecation to consumer teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n2. Mark `channel` with `@deprecated` in [`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts) and [`src/core/order.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts).\n3. Once all downstream services have migrated away from consuming the field, coordinate the removal following the organization's schema version deprecation schedule.\n",
